# Cloudflare Pages headers for the web build.
#
# ── CACHING IS WHAT MAKES "IT UPDATES ITSELF" TRUE OR FALSE ──
#
# The whole appeal of the Activity is that everybody runs whatever was last
# deployed. Our filenames are NOT content-hashed -- OpenDoctrines.wasm is
# always called that -- so an aggressive max-age would pin players to a stale
# build for the length of the cache, and the update would arrive whenever the
# browser felt like it.
#
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate` asks the browser to check every load. That is
# not the same as re-downloading: an unchanged file answers 304 with no body,
# so a returning player pays a round trip rather than six megabytes. A changed
# file arrives immediately. That is exactly the trade this wants.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  # ── NO X-Frame-Options AT ALL, WHICH IS THE POINT ──
  #
  # The game is meant to be framed: by Discord, and by itch.io today. The
  # header's only valid values are DENY and SAMEORIGIN -- both of which would
  # break that -- and ALLOWALL, which this file used to send, is not a real
  # value. It "works" purely because browsers ignore what they cannot parse,
  # which is a bad thing to depend on and reads as deliberate to whoever finds
  # it next.
  #
  # Absence is the standard way to say "framing is allowed". A CSP
  # frame-ancestors list would be the way to restrict it, and is deliberately
  # not set here: under Discord the page is served through the proxy at
  # <id>.discordsays.com rather than framed from this origin directly, so a
  # list written without testing that is a list that blocks the Activity.
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# Correct types, stated rather than assumed: a .wasm served as
# application/octet-stream fails instantiateStreaming and falls back to a
# slower path, or fails outright depending on the browser.
/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm
# ── THE .data BUNDLE'S TYPE IS CHOSEN FOR COMPRESSION ──
#
# Measured against the deployed site, not the local files: the wasm came down
# brotli'd at 3.1 MB and the .data came down at the full 10 MB, because
# Cloudflare compresses by content-type and application/octet-stream is not on
# its list. That doubled the real download, and no amount of looking at
# `ls` would have shown it.
#
# The loader fetches this as an ArrayBuffer and never reads the type, so
# declaring it application/wasm costs nothing and puts it on the compressible
# list. It is a bundle of game data either way.
/*.data
  Content-Type: application/wasm
/*.js
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8
